  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions\">Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions</a></i> </p><p>Similar to the more common <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Electrostaff\" title=\"Electrostaff\">Electrostaff</a>, the Electropole is an electrified melee weapon used primarily by the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Gungans\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Gungans\">Gungans</a> of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Naboo\" title=\"Naboo\">Naboo</a> and the picadors on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Geonosis\" title=\"Geonosis\">Geonosis</a>. Both cultures use the weapon for herding beasts as well as in battle. </p><p>Unlike the standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Electrostaff\" title=\"Electrostaff\">Electrostaff</a> and the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Pike\" title=\"Force Pike\">Force Pike</a>, the Electropole can be thrown like a javelin. Experienced users often keep two or three Electropoles within reach when expecting trouble, one for close combat and the rest to be thrown at the enemy. </p><p><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Gungans\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Gungans\">Gungans</a> are considered proficient with the Electropole if they have the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Simple_Weapons)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)\">Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)</a> feat. An Electropole requires two <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cells\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Energy Cells\">Energy Cells</a> to operate. </p><p><b>Special:</b>&nbsp;Electropoles can be&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Thrown\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Thrown\">Thrown</a> </p>",
